  "solution": {
    "text": "Using graph of<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> ,<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />In the figure, we can see the graph of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0023_dfb7bba53dba.png\" style=\"width:2.85347in;height:1.44028in\" /><br />Clearly,&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is non-differentiable at<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> ( <math><mn>4</mn></math> points)<br />because there are sharp points at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> there are vertical tangents."
